1	# Phase 2 — Type System Design
2	
3	**Status:** Rewritten 2026-04-21 to align with [ADR-003](../ADR-003-reflexivity-as-foundation.md) and [META_MODEL_DESIGN.md](../META_MODEL_DESIGN.md)
4	**Scope:** Declares the Level-2 meta-instance vocabulary (`knm:*`) for the thesis demo.
5	**Depends on:** META_MODEL_DESIGN.md, KNOWLEDGE_NODE_MODEL.md
6	
7	> **This phase is no longer primarily about `types.ts`.** With the reflexive
8	> foundation, the type system lives in the graph as Turtle. The frontend
9	> TypeScript file is a *derived view*. This doc specifies the canonical
10	> graph-native declarations; frontend shape is provided at the end for
11	> reference only.
12	
13	---
14	
15	## What This Phase Covers
16	
17	Declaring the nine domain node types and fourteen domain/system edge types as
18	meta-instances of the Level-1 primitives defined in META_MODEL_DESIGN.
19	
20	Everything in this phase is authored as RDF Turtle and loaded into Jena. The
21	result is a self-describing type system: the types are themselves nodes that
22	the system can query, visualize, and reason over.
23	
24	---
25	
26	## Prefixes
27	
28	```turtle
29	@prefix kn:   <http://knowledgenetwork.local/meta#> .
30	@prefix knm:  <http://knowledgenetwork.local/meta-instances#> .
31	@prefix knd:  <http://knowledgenetwork.local/domain#> .
32	@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
33	@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
34	@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
35	```
36	
37	---
38	
39	## 1. Node Types (9)
40	
41	All node types are `kn:NodeType` instances. They split into two categories:
42	**knowledge** (subject to Level 1–4 filtering) and **organizational** (always
43	visible).
44	
45	### 1.1 Knowledge Node Types (6)
46	
47	```turtle
48	knm:Concept
49	    a              kn:NodeType ;
50	    rdfs:label     "Concept" ;
51	    kn:description "A unit of knowledge — an idea, algorithm, data structure, or technique." ;
52	    kn:category    "knowledge" .
53	
54	knm:Principle
55	    a              kn:NodeType ;
56	    rdfs:label     "Principle" ;
57	    kn:description "A cross-cutting invariant or rule (e.g., Stability, In-Place, Idempotence)." ;
58	    kn:category    "knowledge" .
59	
60	knm:Example
61	    a              kn:NodeType ;
62	    rdfs:label     "Example" ;
63	    kn:description "A specific instance of a concept — a worked case." ;
64	    kn:category    "knowledge" .
65	
66	knm:Assessment
67	    a              kn:NodeType ;
68	    rdfs:label     "Assessment" ;
69	    kn:description "A test, quiz, or exercise that validates concept understanding." ;
70	    kn:category    "knowledge" .
71	
72	knm:Reference
73	    a              kn:NodeType ;
74	    rdfs:label     "Reference" ;
75	    kn:description "An external resource — paper, book chapter, URL." ;
76	    kn:category    "knowledge" .
77	
78	knm:Analogy
79	    a              kn:NodeType ;
80	    rdfs:label     "Analogy" ;
81	    kn:description "A metaphor connecting a concept to an everyday experience." ;
82	    kn:category    "knowledge" .
83	```
84	
85	### 1.2 Organizational Node Types (3)
86	
87	```turtle
88	knm:Program
89	    a              kn:NodeType ;
90	    rdfs:label     "Program" ;
91	    kn:description "A degree program (e.g., CS undergraduate)." ;
92	    kn:category    "organizational" .
93	
94	knm:Course
95	    a              kn:NodeType ;
96	    rdfs:label     "Course" ;
97	    kn:description "A course within a program (e.g., CS101)." ;
98	    kn:category    "organizational" .
99	
100	knm:Professor
101	    a              kn:NodeType ;
102	    rdfs:label     "Professor" ;
103	    kn:description "A teaching staff member." ;
104	    kn:category    "organizational" .
105	```
106	
107	### 1.3 Artifact Node Type (supporting)
108	
109	```turtle
110	knm:Artifact
111	    a              kn:NodeType ;
112	    rdfs:label     "Artifact" ;
113	    kn:description "A file attachment (PDF, image, code file)." ;
114	    kn:category    "supporting" .
115	```
116	
117	---
118	
119	## 2. Edge Types (14 + 1 derived)
120	
121	All edge types are `kn:EdgeType` instances. Each declares:
122	
123	- Its category (`"domain"` or `"system"`) via `kn:edge_category`
124	- Its OWL characteristic (`owl:TransitiveProperty`, `owl:SymmetricProperty`,
125	  or plain `owl:ObjectProperty`)
126	- `kn:domain` and `kn:range` (allowed source/target types)
127	- Inverse edges where applicable
128	
129	### 2.1 Domain Edges (13 authored + 1 derived)
130	
131	```turtle
132	knm:prerequisite_of
133	    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:TransitiveProperty ;
134	    rdfs:label           "prerequisite of" ;
135	    kn:description       "Source must be understood before target." ;
136	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
137	    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
138	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
139	
140	knm:generalizes
141	    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:TransitiveProperty ;
142	    rdfs:label           "generalizes" ;
143	    kn:description       "Source is a more general form of target." ;
144	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
145	    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
146	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
147	
148	knm:is_instance_of
149	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
150	    rdfs:label           "is instance of" ;
151	    kn:description       "Source is a specific occurrence of target." ;
152	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
153	    kn:domain            knm:Example ;
154	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
155	
156	knm:is_component_of
157	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
158	    rdfs:label           "is component of" ;
159	    kn:description       "Source is a conceptual part of target (semantic, not lifecycle)." ;
160	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
161	    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
162	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
163	
164	knm:builds_on
165	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
166	    rdfs:label           "builds on" ;
167	    kn:description       "Source extends or refines target." ;
168	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
169	    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
170	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
171	
172	knm:contradicts
173	    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:SymmetricProperty ;
174	    rdfs:label           "contradicts" ;
175	    kn:description       "Source and target are in logical tension." ;
176	    kn:edge_category     "domain" .
177	
178	knm:is_analogous_to
179	    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:SymmetricProperty ;
180	    rdfs:label           "is analogous to" ;
181	    kn:description       "Source and target share structural similarity." ;
182	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
183	    kn:domain            knm:Analogy ;
184	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
185	
186	knm:applies_in
187	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
188	    rdfs:label           "applies in" ;
189	    kn:description       "Source is used in the context of target." ;
190	    kn:edge_category     "domain" .
191	
192	knm:commonly_conflated_with
193	    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:SymmetricProperty ;
194	    rdfs:label           "commonly conflated with" ;
195	    kn:description       "Source and target are frequently but incorrectly treated as the same." ;
196	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
197	    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
198	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
199	
200	knm:demonstrates
201	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
202	    rdfs:label           "demonstrates" ;
203	    kn:description       "Source concept demonstrates target principle." ;
204	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
205	    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
206	    kn:range             knm:Principle ;
207	    owl:inverseOf        knm:is_demonstrated_by .
208	
209	knm:is_demonstrated_by
210	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
211	    rdfs:label           "is demonstrated by" ;
212	    kn:description       "Target principle is demonstrated by source concept." ;
213	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
214	    kn:domain            knm:Principle ;
215	    kn:range             knm:Concept ;
216	    owl:inverseOf        knm:demonstrates .
217	
218	knm:teaches
219	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
220	    rdfs:label           "teaches" ;
221	    kn:description       "Professor teaches a course." ;
222	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
223	    kn:domain            knm:Professor ;
224	    kn:range             knm:Course .
225	
226	knm:contains
227	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
228	    rdfs:label           "contains" ;
229	    kn:description       "Organizational grouping (user-authored, unlike knm:sys_contains)." ;
230	    kn:edge_category     "domain" .
231	```
232	
233	### 2.2 Derived Edge (inference output)
234	
235	```turtle
236	knm:assesses
237	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
238	    rdfs:label           "assesses" ;
239	    kn:description       "An assessment assesses a concept. Derived from Assessment knm:applies_in Concept." ;
240	    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
241	    kn:derived           true ;
242	    kn:domain            knm:Assessment ;
243	    kn:range             knm:Concept .
244	```
245	
246	The `kn:derived true` flag signals that edges of this type are produced by
247	inference, not hand-authored. The projection rule lives in the Jena rule set
248	(see Phase 5 — inference backend).
249	
250	### 2.3 System Edge (1)
251	
252	```turtle
253	knm:sys_contains
254	    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
255	    rdfs:label           "system contains" ;
256	    kn:description       "Lifecycle ownership — cascade, exclusive, auto-authored." ;
257	    kn:edge_category     "system" ;
258	    kn:default_on_delete "cascade" ;
259	    kn:default_exclusive true ;
260	    kn:user_editable     false .
261	```
262	
263	Per-instance properties (`kn:on_delete`, `kn:exclusive`, `kn:auto_created`,
264	`kn:user_editable`) override these defaults on individual edge nodes.
265	
266	---
267	
268	## 3. Property Descriptors
269	
270	Per META_MODEL_DESIGN §"Property Representation", every domain-specific
271	property has a `knm:PropertyDescriptor` declaration. Values still live as
272	plain triples; the descriptor is the definition.
273	
274	```turtle
275	knm:format
276	    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
277	    rdfs:label           "format" ;
278	    kn:description       "Assessment format — distinguishes test/quiz/exercise." ;
279	    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
280	    kn:allowed_values    ( "test" "quiz" "exercise" ) ;
281	    kn:applies_to        knm:Assessment .
282	
283	knm:url
284	    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
285	    rdfs:label           "url" ;
286	    kn:description       "External resource URL." ;
287	    kn:data_type         xsd:anyURI ;
288	    kn:applies_to        knm:Reference .
289	
290	knm:citation
291	    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
292	    rdfs:label           "citation" ;
293	    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
294	    kn:applies_to        knm:Reference .
295	
296	knm:course_code
297	    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
298	    rdfs:label           "course code" ;
299	    kn:description       "Short identifier (e.g., 'CS101')." ;
300	    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
301	    kn:applies_to        knm:Course .
302	
303	knm:department
304	    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
305	    rdfs:label           "department" ;
306	    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
307	    kn:applies_to        knm:Professor .
308	```
309	
310	Semantics of `allowed_values` are enforced by the validation engine
311	(Phase 6), not by OWL itself — OWL 2 RL has no closed-world enumeration.
312	
313	---
314	
315	## 4. Visual Styles
316	
317	Per META_MODEL_DESIGN §"Visual Style", styles are subgraphs with cascading
318	via `kn:subtype_of`. Root abstract style:
319	
320	```turtle
321	knm:DefaultNodeStyle
322	    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
323	    kn:color             "#CBD5E1" ;
324	    kn:border_color      "#64748B" ;
325	    kn:shape             "rounded_rectangle" ;
326	    kn:label_position    "center" .
327	
328	knm:DefaultEdgeStyle
329	    a                    kn:EdgeVisualStyle ;
330	    kn:color             "#94A3B8" ;
331	    kn:line_style        "solid" ;
332	    kn:arrow_head        "triangle" ;
333	    kn:width             1.5 .
334	```
335	
336	### Node styles
337	
338	```turtle
339	knm:ConceptStyle
340	    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
341	    kn:subtype_of        knm:DefaultNodeStyle ;
342	    kn:applies_to        knm:Concept ;
343	    kn:color             "#DBEAFE" ;           # blue-100
344	    kn:border_color      "#60A5FA" .           # blue-400
345	
346	knm:PrincipleStyle
347	    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
348	    kn:subtype_of        knm:DefaultNodeStyle ;
349	    kn:applies_to        knm:Principle ;
350	    kn:color             "#EDE9FE" ;           # violet-100
351	    kn:border_color      "#A78BFA" .
352	
353	knm:ExampleStyle
354	    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
355	    kn:subtype_of        knm:DefaultNodeStyle ;
356	    kn:applies_to        knm:Example ;
357	    kn:color             "#D1FAE5" ;           # emerald-100
358	    kn:border_color      "#34D399" ;
359	    kn:badge             "eg" .
360	
361	knm:AssessmentTestStyle
362	    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
363	    kn:subtype_of        knm:DefaultNodeStyle ;
364	    kn:applies_to        knm:Assessment ;
365	    kn:filter_property   knm:format ;
366	    kn:filter_value      "test" ;
367	    kn:color             "#FEE2E2" ;
368	    kn:border_color      "#F87171" ;
369	    kn:badge             "✓" .
370	
371	knm:AssessmentQuizStyle
372	    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
373	    kn:subtype_of        knm:DefaultNodeStyle ;
374	    kn:applies_to        knm:Assessment ;
375	    kn:filter_property   knm:format ;
376	    kn:filter_value      "quiz" ;
377	    kn:color             "#FFEDD5" ;
378	    kn:border_color      "#FB923C" ;
379	    kn:badge             "?" .
380	
381	knm:AssessmentExerciseStyle
382	    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
383	    kn:subtype_of        knm:DefaultNodeStyle ;
