462	    kn:line_style        "dotted" ;
463	    kn:width             1 ;
464	    kn:opacity           0.4 ;
465	    kn:hidden_by_default true .
466	```
467	
468	Style resolution: the UI walks `kn:subtype_of` upward and takes the first
469	defined value for each property (CSS-specificity semantics). Filter
470	properties (`kn:filter_property`/`kn:filter_value`) allow variant styling of
471	the same node type based on property values (e.g., Assessment formats).
472	
473	---
474	
475	## 5. Frontend TypeScript View
476	
477	The backend queries Jena and projects results into these TypeScript shapes
478	for the React UI. These types are **derived** — the canonical source is the
479	Turtle above.
480	
481	```typescript
482	// derived from knm:* declarations; regenerated when the type system changes
483	export type EducationNodeType =
484	  | 'Concept'
485	  | 'Principle'
486	  | 'Example'
487	  | 'Assessment'
488	  | 'Reference'
489	  | 'Analogy'
490	  | 'Program'
491	  | 'Course'
492	  | 'Professor'
493	
494	export type DomainEdgeType =
495	  | 'prerequisite_of'
496	  | 'generalizes'
497	  | 'is_instance_of'
498	  | 'is_component_of'
499	  | 'builds_on'
500	  | 'contradicts'
501	  | 'is_analogous_to'
502	  | 'applies_in'
503	  | 'commonly_conflated_with'
504	  | 'demonstrates'
505	  | 'is_demonstrated_by'
506	  | 'teaches'
507	  | 'contains'
508	  | 'assesses'  // derived
509	
510	export type SystemEdgeType = 'sys_contains'
511	
512	export interface KnowledgeNode {
513	  id: string
514	  label: string
515	  type: EducationNodeType
516	  description?: string
517	  documentId?: string
518	  artifacts: Artifact[]
519	  // type-specific properties
520	  format?: 'test' | 'quiz' | 'exercise'   // Assessment
521	  url?: string                             // Reference
522	  citation?: string                        // Reference
523	  courseCode?: string                      // Course
524	  department?: string                      // Professor
525	}
526	
527	export interface KnowledgeEdge {
528	  id: string
529	  source: string
530	  target: string
531	  type: DomainEdgeType | SystemEdgeType
532	  category: 'system' | 'domain'
533	  inferred?: boolean
534	  properties?: {
535	    onDelete?: 'cascade' | 'detach' | 'prevent'
536	    exclusive?: boolean
537	    autoCreated?: boolean
538	    userEditable?: boolean
539	  }
540	}
541	```
542	
543	Generation strategy (deferred to implementation): either hand-maintain this
544	file in sync with Turtle declarations, or generate it from a SPARQL query
545	over `knm:*` at build time. For the thesis demo, hand-maintained is fine.
546	
547	---
548	
549	## 6. Loading Order
550	
551	The Turtle files load into Jena in this order (each layer depends on the
552	previous):
553	
554	1. `meta.ttl` — Level 1 primitives (see META_MODEL_DESIGN)
555	2. `meta-instances.ttl` — this document: nine node types + fourteen edge types + property descriptors + visual styles
556	3. `domain.ttl` — Level 3: 559 demo nodes and their edges
557	4. `rules.ttl` — projection rules (reified ↔ classical) + OWL 2 RL rule set
558	5. Inference pass — Jena computes transitive closures, symmetric pairs, and `knm:assesses` derivations
559	
560	---
561	
562	## 7. Validation Checklist
563	
564	- [ ] All nine node types load and query back as `kn:NodeType` instances
565	- [ ] All fourteen edge types load with correct `kn:edge_category`
566	- [ ] OWL characteristics (`owl:TransitiveProperty`, `owl:SymmetricProperty`,
567	      `owl:inverseOf`) propagate through the reasoner
568	- [ ] Visual style subgraph resolves via `kn:subtype_of` walk
569	- [ ] `knm:assesses` edges appear after inference runs on sample domain data
570	- [ ] Frontend-derived TypeScript types compile and render styled nodes
571	- [ ] `kn:edge_category` query correctly separates system from domain edges
572	
573	---
574	
575	## 8. Changed from Pre-Pivot Version
576	
577	- TypeScript unions are no longer authoritative — Turtle declarations are.
578	- Edge category is a property of the edge type node, not a URI prefix.
579	- Visual styles are subgraphs, not a hard-coded table in the frontend.
580	- Assessment format is a property descriptor, not a TypeScript literal type.
581	- OWL characteristics (`TransitiveProperty`, `SymmetricProperty`) are declared
582	  on the edge type directly in OWL, not mirrored as a `owlType` string on
583	  individual edges.
584	- Artifact is now a real `knm:NodeType`, not an inline struct on `KnowledgeNode`.
585	
586	## 9. Files to Change in Implementation
587	
588	| File | Change |
589	|---|---|
590	| `data/meta.ttl` | New — Level-1 primitives (from META_MODEL_DESIGN) |
591	| `data/meta-instances.ttl` | New — contents of §1–§4 of this doc |
592	| `data/rules.ttl` | New — projection + OWL 2 RL rules |
593	| `src/types.ts` | Rewrite per §5 |
594	| `src/components/KGNode.tsx` | Read visual style from backend instead of hard-coded table |
595	| `src/components/KGEdge.tsx` | Read visual style from backend |
596	
597	Hard-coded visual tables in the current frontend become fallback defaults only.
598

