# Phase 2 — Type System Design

**Status:** Rewritten 2026-04-21 to align with [ADR-003](../ADR-003-reflexivity-as-foundation.md) and [META_MODEL_DESIGN.md](../META_MODEL_DESIGN.md)
**Scope:** Declares the Level-2 meta-instance vocabulary (`knm:*`) for the thesis demo.
**Depends on:** META_MODEL_DESIGN.md, KNOWLEDGE_NODE_MODEL.md

> **This phase is no longer primarily about `types.ts`.** With the reflexive
> foundation, the type system lives in the graph as Turtle. The frontend
> TypeScript file is a *derived view*. This doc specifies the canonical
> graph-native declarations; frontend shape is provided at the end for
> reference only.

---

## What This Phase Covers

Declaring the nine domain node types and fourteen domain/system edge types as
meta-instances of the Level-1 primitives defined in META_MODEL_DESIGN.

Everything in this phase is authored as RDF Turtle and loaded into Jena. The
result is a self-describing type system: the types are themselves nodes that
the system can query, visualize, and reason over.

---

## Prefixes

```turtle
@prefix kn:   <http://knowledgenetwork.local/meta#> .
@prefix knm:  <http://knowledgenetwork.local/meta-instances#> .
@prefix knd:  <http://knowledgenetwork.local/domain#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
```

---

## 1. Node Types (9)

All node types are `kn:NodeType` instances. They split into two categories:
**knowledge** (subject to Level 1–4 filtering) and **organizational** (always
visible).

### 1.1 Knowledge Node Types (6)

```turtle
knm:Concept
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Concept" ;
    kn:description "A unit of knowledge — an idea, algorithm, data structure, or technique." ;
    kn:category    "knowledge" .

knm:Principle
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Principle" ;
    kn:description "A cross-cutting invariant or rule (e.g., Stability, In-Place, Idempotence)." ;
    kn:category    "knowledge" .

knm:Example
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Example" ;
    kn:description "A specific instance of a concept — a worked case." ;
    kn:category    "knowledge" .

knm:Assessment
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Assessment" ;
    kn:description "A test, quiz, or exercise that validates concept understanding." ;
    kn:category    "knowledge" .

knm:Reference
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Reference" ;
    kn:description "An external resource — paper, book chapter, URL." ;
    kn:category    "knowledge" .

knm:Analogy
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Analogy" ;
    kn:description "A metaphor connecting a concept to an everyday experience." ;
    kn:category    "knowledge" .
```

### 1.2 Organizational Node Types (3)

```turtle
knm:Program
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Program" ;
    kn:description "A degree program (e.g., CS undergraduate)." ;
    kn:category    "organizational" .

knm:Course
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Course" ;
    kn:description "A course within a program (e.g., CS101)." ;
    kn:category    "organizational" .

knm:Professor
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Professor" ;
    kn:description "A teaching staff member." ;
    kn:category    "organizational" .
```

### 1.3 Artifact Node Type (supporting)

```turtle
knm:Artifact
    a              kn:NodeType ;
    rdfs:label     "Artifact" ;
    kn:description "A file attachment (PDF, image, code file)." ;
    kn:category    "supporting" .
```

---

## 2. Edge Types (14 + 1 derived)

All edge types are `kn:EdgeType` instances. Each declares:

- Its category (`"domain"` or `"system"`) via `kn:edge_category`
- Its OWL characteristic (`owl:TransitiveProperty`, `owl:SymmetricProperty`,
  or plain `owl:ObjectProperty`)
- `kn:domain` and `kn:range` (allowed source/target types)
- Inverse edges where applicable

### 2.1 Domain Edges (13 authored + 1 derived)

```turtle
knm:prerequisite_of
    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label           "prerequisite of" ;
    kn:description       "Source must be understood before target." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .

knm:generalizes
    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label           "generalizes" ;
    kn:description       "Source is a more general form of target." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .

knm:is_instance_of
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "is instance of" ;
    kn:description       "Source is a specific occurrence of target." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Example ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .

knm:is_component_of
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "is component of" ;
    kn:description       "Source is a conceptual part of target (semantic, not lifecycle)." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .

knm:builds_on
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "builds on" ;
    kn:description       "Source extends or refines target." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .

knm:contradicts
    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label           "contradicts" ;
    kn:description       "Source and target are in logical tension." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" .

knm:is_analogous_to
    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label           "is analogous to" ;
    kn:description       "Source and target share structural similarity." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Analogy ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .

knm:applies_in
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "applies in" ;
    kn:description       "Source is used in the context of target." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" .

knm:commonly_conflated_with
    a                    kn:EdgeType , owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label           "commonly conflated with" ;
    kn:description       "Source and target are frequently but incorrectly treated as the same." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .

knm:demonstrates
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "demonstrates" ;
    kn:description       "Source concept demonstrates target principle." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Concept ;
    kn:range             knm:Principle ;
    owl:inverseOf        knm:is_demonstrated_by .

knm:is_demonstrated_by
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "is demonstrated by" ;
    kn:description       "Target principle is demonstrated by source concept." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Principle ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept ;
    owl:inverseOf        knm:demonstrates .

knm:teaches
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "teaches" ;
    kn:description       "Professor teaches a course." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:domain            knm:Professor ;
    kn:range             knm:Course .

knm:contains
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "contains" ;
    kn:description       "Organizational grouping (user-authored, unlike knm:sys_contains)." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" .
```

### 2.2 Derived Edge (inference output)

```turtle
knm:assesses
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "assesses" ;
    kn:description       "An assessment assesses a concept. Derived from Assessment knm:applies_in Concept." ;
    kn:edge_category     "domain" ;
    kn:derived           true ;
    kn:domain            knm:Assessment ;
    kn:range             knm:Concept .
```

The `kn:derived true` flag signals that edges of this type are produced by
inference, not hand-authored. The projection rule lives in the Jena rule set
(see Phase 5 — inference backend).

### 2.3 System Edge (1)

```turtle
knm:sys_contains
    a                    kn:EdgeType ;
    rdfs:label           "system contains" ;
    kn:description       "Lifecycle ownership — cascade, exclusive, auto-authored." ;
    kn:edge_category     "system" ;
    kn:default_on_delete "cascade" ;
    kn:default_exclusive true ;
    kn:user_editable     false .
```

Per-instance properties (`kn:on_delete`, `kn:exclusive`, `kn:auto_created`,
`kn:user_editable`) override these defaults on individual edge nodes.

---

## 3. Property Descriptors

Per META_MODEL_DESIGN §"Property Representation", every domain-specific
property has a `knm:PropertyDescriptor` declaration. Values still live as
plain triples; the descriptor is the definition.

```turtle
knm:format
    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label           "format" ;
    kn:description       "Assessment format — distinguishes test/quiz/exercise." ;
    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
    kn:allowed_values    ( "test" "quiz" "exercise" ) ;
    kn:applies_to        knm:Assessment .

knm:url
    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label           "url" ;
    kn:description       "External resource URL." ;
    kn:data_type         xsd:anyURI ;
    kn:applies_to        knm:Reference .

knm:citation
    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label           "citation" ;
    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
    kn:applies_to        knm:Reference .

knm:course_code
    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label           "course code" ;
    kn:description       "Short identifier (e.g., 'CS101')." ;
    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
    kn:applies_to        knm:Course .

knm:department
    a                    knm:PropertyDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label           "department" ;
    kn:data_type         xsd:string ;
    kn:applies_to        knm:Professor .
```

Semantics of `allowed_values` are enforced by the validation engine
(Phase 6), not by OWL itself — OWL 2 RL has no closed-world enumeration.

---

## 4. Visual Styles

Per META_MODEL_DESIGN §"Visual Style", styles are subgraphs with cascading
via `kn:subtype_of`. Root abstract style:

```turtle
knm:DefaultNodeStyle
    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
    kn:color             "#CBD5E1" ;
    kn:border_color      "#64748B" ;
    kn:shape             "rounded_rectangle" ;
    kn:label_position    "center" .

knm:DefaultEdgeStyle
    a                    kn:EdgeVisualStyle ;
    kn:color             "#94A3B8" ;
    kn:line_style        "solid" ;
    kn:arrow_head        "triangle" ;
    kn:width             1.5 .
```

### Node styles

```turtle
knm:ConceptStyle
    a                    kn:NodeVisualStyle ;
    kn:subtype_of        knm:DefaultNodeStyle ;
    kn:applies_to        knm:Concept ;
    kn:color             "#DBEAFE" ;           # blue-100
    kn:border_color      "#60A5FA" .           # blue-400

knm:PrincipleStyle
